== queued batch depth ==
every calibration estimate gets the depth the policy owes it: true
no calibration estimate ever yields a depth below 1: true
no calibration estimate ever yields a depth above the cap: true

== autotune_timing spelling ==
"queued" selects the queued objective: true
"isolated" selects the isolated objective: true
the spelling is case- and space-insensitive: true
a misspelling is refused rather than defaulted: true

== the instrument's two modes ==
both modes returned a positive finite per-launch time: true
isolated timing dispatched one launch per timed run, warmup included: true
queued timing dispatched more launches than isolated timing did: true
isolated reading is a per-launch time: PASS
queued reading is a per-launch time: PASS
queued timing does not read above isolated timing: PASS
queued timing's wall cost is bounded by the budget, not by the batch depth: PASS
